    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Let me review what I've done:\n\n1. I identified the repeated pattern in the invoicing/parsing.py file where several functions were checking for missing or blank header fields and raising ParseError with the same message format.\n\n2. I created a helper function `_get_required_header()` that encapsulates this logic:\n   - Takes a headers dictionary and a key to look up\n   - Gets the value for that key from headers\n   - Checks if the value is None or blank (empty or only whitespace)\n   - Raises ParseError with the message \"missing field: {key}\" if the field is missing or blank\n   - Returns the stripped value if it exists and is not blank\n\n3. I refactored the `parse_number`, `parse_customer`, and `parse_issued` functions to use this helper function instead of the repeated code.\n\n4. The `parse_issued` function required a slight modification because it also needs to parse the date, but I preserved the original behavior for that case.\n\n5. I verified that all existing tests still pass, confirming that the refactoring maintains the same behavior.\n\nThe refactoring is clean, maintains all existing functionality, and eliminates the code duplication while keeping the same error messages and behavior.\n",
